course: dictionary
lesson: 3609
title: Filament: a thin thread
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A filament is a very thin thread or wire. You can work out its meaning from the words around it, which are its context. «An LED bulb gives the same light as an old filament bulb with far less electricity.» The old bulb is the one with a filament, and it needs more electricity, so the filament must be a part of the old bulb that makes the light.
explain: Some words are used in different subjects, so the context tells you which meaning is right. In science, a filament can be the glowing wire in a bulb. In biology, it can be a thin thread in a plant or a flower. Ask yourself: what is this thing being talked about, and what is it doing?
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «The filament glows when electricity passes through it» still makes sense if you think of a thin wire. If the meaning does not fit, read on, look for more clues, or ask a teacher or use a dictionary.
fact: A filament is a very thin thread or wire.
fact: In an old-style light bulb, the filament is the thin wire that glows when electricity passes through it.
fact: In a flower, a filament is the thin stalk that holds up the anther.
fact: The plastic thread used in a 3D printer is also called a filament.
fact: «Filament» is a noun. You can say a filament and filaments.
exercise: «An LED bulb gives the same light as an old filament bulb with far less electricity.» In this sentence, what is a filament? | The glass cover of a light | The plastic from a 3D printer | The switch on the wall | *The thin wire that glows in an old bulb
exercise: A filament is a very thin thread. Which of these is most like a filament? | *A strand of cotton | A large rock | A brick | A puddle
exercise: «The smell is the fine filament, the telegraphic current.» Which word is the clue that filament means something thin? | *fine | the | current | smell
test: In a flower, what is the filament part of? | *The stamen, where it holds up the anther | The root | The petal | A stem
test: Which words in «An LED bulb gives the same light as an old filament bulb with far less electricity» tell you the filament is part of an old bulb? | *The words old filament bulb | The word light | The word electricity | The word LED
exam: Which meaning of filament is used when you say, «The plastic filament feeds into the 3D printer»? | A thin thread in a fungus | *The plastic thread used in a 3D printer | A bulb wire that glows | The stamen in a flower
